I am working on a Machine Learning / AI project to analyze Instagram posts, predict engagement and provide recommendations using various features- based on User Behavioral Data ( user comment analysis ). The dataset I use is a merged dataset with post-level, comment-level, and follower-level information, enhanced with sentiment scores and high-value follower indicators.

### Dataset Description:
The dataset contains the following fields (columns):

- post_id: Unique identifier of the Instagram post
- owner_id: Owner user ID of the post
- timestamp: UNIX timestamp of the post creation
- likes: Number of likes on the post
- comments_count: Number of comments on the post
- caption: Text caption of the post
- hashtags: Hashtags used in the post
- location_id: Location identifier
- media_type: Type of media (e.g., image, video)
- username: Username of the post owner
- shortcode: Instagram shortcode for the post URL
- location: Location name
- is_private: Boolean indicating if the account is private
- is_verified: Boolean indicating if the account is verified
- mentions: Users mentioned in the caption
- Category: Category of the content (e.g., fashion, food)
- #Followers, #Followees, #Posts: Owner’s follower/following/post counts
- comment_text: Text of the comment on the post
- comment_owner_username: Username of the commenter
- comment_likes: Number of likes on the comment
- comment_timestamp: Timestamp of the comment
- caption_length: Length of the caption text in characters
- num_hashtags: Number of hashtags in the caption
- has_mention, has_url: Booleans if caption has mentions or URLs
- follower_adjusted_likes, follower_adjusted_comments: Engagement metrics adjusted by followers
- engagement_rate, hashtags_agg, engagement_frequency, influence_score, content_interaction, comment_engagement_ratio: Various engagement and influence metrics
- comment_length: Length of comment text
- has_emoji: Boolean if comment has emoji
- category_beauty, category_family, ..., category_travel: Binary category flags
- user_id_encoded: Encoded user ID feature
- engagement_binary, engagement_probability: Engagement classification and prediction probabilities
- sentiment, sentiment_confidence, sentiment_positive, sentiment_negative, sentiment_neutral: Sentiment analysis results per comment
- is_high_value_follower: Boolean indicator if the commenter is a high-value follower
- comment_likes_sum: Sum of likes on comments
- sentiment_positive_post, sentiment_negative_post, sentiment_neutral_post, avg_comment_sentiment: Aggregated post-level sentiment scores
- num_comments: Number of comments on the post
- sentiment_weighted_engagement: Target variable representing engagement weighted by sentiment

